{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>And He said, I will cause all My goodness to pass before your face.</b> This too is a filling out of the matter regarding what He said, 'Also this thing that you spoke I will do,' and regarding what he asked, 'Show me, I pray, Your glory' — He said to him, 'You cannot see My face.' When Moses heard this, he thought in his heart and said: perhaps His mind is not clear with me, and He does not wish to show me anything. And He said immediately, 'Behold, a place is with Me,' etc., 'and you shall see My back.' And one may say: 'Show me, I pray, Your glory' does not mean the glory itself, for we find, 'And Moses hid his face, for he feared to gaze upon Elohim.' Rather, this is what it says: 'Show me, I pray, Your glory' — by the cutting of a covenant, that You have agreed to what I asked of You. And so He did, as it is written, <b>And He said, I will cause all My goodness to pass before your face</b>, etc. <b>I will cause to pass</b> — I will proclaim, as in 'and they passed a proclamation through the camp.'" "<b>All My goodness.</b> Every measure of My goodness, both for the righteous and for the wicked. 'And I will proclaim by the name of HaShem before you' — Rashi explained: in the same manner as you see Me wrapped and reciting, etc. That is what is written at the beginning of the passage, 'HaShem descended in the cloud' — He wrapped Himself in the cloud of His glory. And so it is that we find Him wrapped in cloud: 'He makes clouds His garment, mist His cloak.'" "<b>And I will grant grace to whom I grant grace.</b> He did not agree to grant atonement altogether, and this refers back to what was said above: 'And I and Your people shall be distinct,' etc."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:01:47.697341566Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}